KG42.register("rules-175eac5183207daa1df66224",{"id":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R006","paper":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Demand submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The flexible consumer may submit a requested-load bid with a bid price and allow the requested load to be served over a set of delivery nodes. Scope: The single flexible consumer analyzed in the load-disaggregation market formulation.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.demand under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"The single flexible consumer analyzed in the load-disaggregation market formulation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-T001","symbol":"\\bar d","meaning":"Requested load submitted in the flexible consumer's bid; the source uses it as the requested-load quantity for the bid.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\bar d"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-T002","symbol":"\\alpha^{d}","meaning":"Bid price submitted with the flexible consumer's requested load.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\alpha^{d}"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-T003","symbol":"\\mathcal{N}_{d}","meaning":"Set of delivery nodes at which the requested load may be served; the source states N_d subset N.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\mathcal{N}_{d}\\subseteq\\mathcal{N}"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g01-e011"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R006-T004","symbol":"\\mathcal{N}","meaning":"Set of all network nodes, used as the ambient node set in the source statement N_d subset N.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\mathcal{N}"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g01-e011"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The flexible consumer may submit a requested-load bid with a bid price and allow the requested load to be served over a set of delivery nodes. Scope: The single flexible consumer analyzed in the load-disaggregation market formulation.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The delivery nodes offered for the requested load form a subset of the network nodes.","expression":"\\mathcal{N}_{d}\\subseteq\\mathcal{N}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R006-T003","v141-c-R006-T004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g01-e011"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e038","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Basic formulation with flexible consumers","anchor_text":"2) Understanding the effect of transmission capacity on prices will become relevant for the formulat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We now expand the previous clearing formulation by incorporating flexible consumers; specifically, we consider flexible consumers that offer load-shifting flexibility by exploiting the availability of multiple DaCes placed at different nodes. For simplicity in the presentation, we consider a single flexible consumer. Suppose that this consumer submits a bid for requested load \\bar{d} with bid price \\alpha^{d}; the requested load can be served/delivered at a set of nodes \\mathcal{N}_{d}\\subseteq\\mathcal{N}. Each node n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d} receives a partial load d_{n}\\ge 0; the total load served to the consumer is \\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d}}d_{n} and satisfies \\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}_{d}}d_{n}\\le\\bar{d} (total load served cannot exceed the requested load)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M02-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1 Basic notation and terminology","anchor_text":"our formulation does not enforce a hard minimum load (load shedding be is allowed to all levels). Ho","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A standard (inflexible) consumer requests that the cleared load d_j is delivered at a single node n(j) \\in \\mathcal{N}. A flexible consumer (a DaCe owner), on the other hand, offers the possibility that the cleared load d_j is delivered at a set of possible nodes \\mathcal{N}_{d} \\subseteq N; in other words, the cleared load d_j can be disaggregated and individual portions are delivered at different nodes. We will see that this load disaggregation scheme can be seen as a spatial, load-shifting mechanism that can be modeled using virtual links. For simplicity, we will not make a distinction between DaCe owners and inflexible consumers. This is because an inflexible consumer can be modeled as a flexible consumer with \\mathcal{N}_{d}=\\{n(j)\\} (it offers one node option for the load to be delivered)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The source describes the flexible consumer's requested load and bid price as submitted bid inputs, not as a bidding-stage optimization variable or decision problem in this rule; the clearing allocation variables d_n belong to the clearing relation v141-c-R007 and are not re-declared here.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-bidding","v141-a-M02-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e038","quote":"For simplicity in the presentation, we consider a single flexible consumer. Suppose that this consumer submits a bid for requested load \\bar{d} with bid price \\alpha^{d}; the requested load can be served/delivered at a set of nodes \\mathcal{N}_{d}\\subseteq\\mathcal{N}."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"d1d8db4a46e83c2a179423e069308da8e6f8eab9c33bea6e635829f872ee62c2","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The frozen rule is a bidding-stage demand-submission relation. The quoted source (v141-b-g01-e038, with same-mechanism support from v141-b-g01-e011 for the offered-node set) defines a flexible consumer's requested-load bid with bid price and a delivery-node set N_d subset N. This patch therefore declares the submitted bid inputs as parameters under bidding.demand and formalizes only the supported offered-node subset relation. The partial-load variables d_n and the aggregate condition sum_{n in N_d} d_n \u003c= bar d are clearing-stage constructs owned by the separate clearing relation v141-c-R007 in the frozen inventory; they are not re-declared here under the bidding node. B evidence used here remains UNREVIEWED candidate support, not an independently verified source audit.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Existing procedural bid-submission constraint is retained with its frozen node membership; it remains not_formalized as a single equation because the source states the bid and delivery allowance in prose."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-T001","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Requested load is a submitted bid input under bidding.demand; no edge is present in the frozen rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-T002","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Bid price is a submitted bid input under bidding.demand; no edge is present in the frozen rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-T003","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The offered delivery-node set is part of the demand bid; no edge is present in the frozen rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-T004","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The ambient network node set is used only to state the source-supported offered-node subset N_d subset N within this bidding rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The formalized offered-node subset relation is a property of the demand bid; it uses the existing bidding.demand node and does not add or alter frozen edges."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
